1
00:01:40,170 --> 00:01:41,340
Red and Blue, ready?

2
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:42,880
Let us start!

3
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:48,380
Keerthi! Keerthi! Keerthi!

4
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:50,590
Come on, Keerthi!

5
00:01:50,670 --> 00:01:53,920
Keerthi! Keerthi! Keerthi!

6
00:01:58,340 --> 00:02:01,220
Sister, come on! Nail it!

7
00:02:08,669 --> 00:02:09,590
Come on, slam her!

8
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:14,920
-Hey!
-Wow!

9
00:02:16,290 --> 00:02:18,670
Come on, grab her leg!

10
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:22,290
Come on, grab her! Slam her!

11
00:02:26,710 --> 00:02:28,420
Yes!

12
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,000
Come on, slam her!

13
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:36,210
Wow!

14
00:02:41,670 --> 00:02:43,300
-Congratulations!
-Thank you, sir.

15
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:44,460
Well done!

16
00:02:45,210 --> 00:02:46,290
The next plan of our academy

17
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:48,210
is to conduct
the Submission Wrestling Tournament.

18
00:02:48,380 --> 00:02:49,960
Players from other towns will participate.

19
00:02:50,210 --> 00:02:51,670
But I expect your performance

20
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:53,330
to stand out from others. Okay?

21
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:54,750
-Sure, sir.
-Good!

22
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:57,210
-The last slam where you nailed her.
-Yes.

23
00:02:57,290 --> 00:02:59,250
You applied my technique with diligence.

24
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:00,840
Uncle, there's no match for you.

25
00:03:01,290 --> 00:03:02,370
You played well, dear!

26
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:05,620
Who is home?

27
00:03:06,210 --> 00:03:07,420
I wonder who has arrived.

28
00:03:10,090 --> 00:03:11,050
What's wrong with you?

29
00:03:20,210 --> 00:03:22,540
Please wait.
I'll get her changed into a saree.

30
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:23,590
Not necessary.

31
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,380
We have seen enough.

32
00:03:26,290 --> 00:03:28,710
The broker told us
that she quit wrestling.

33
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:31,720
Once she's married, 
she won't indulge in wrestling.

34
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,250
Why are you making her quit wrestling?

35
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:35,120
If everyone gets married, 

36
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:37,550
then who will win medals for our nation?

37
00:03:38,130 --> 00:03:39,630
I'll get straight to the point.

38
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:42,500
You could get your younger daughter
married to my son.

39
00:03:43,090 --> 00:03:45,090
We can fix a date
during the upcoming auspicious day.

40
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:54,090
-You may leave.
-Oh, God!

41
00:03:54,750 --> 00:03:56,000
Why would you do such a thing, mom?

42
00:03:56,130 --> 00:03:58,510
They said the girl would quit wrestling
after the marriage.

43
00:03:58,590 --> 00:04:01,340
How could you lead a life with a wrestler?

44
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:03,050
If she slams you, 
you will die on the spot!

45
00:04:03,250 --> 00:04:05,210
She won't stop with you.
She'll slam me as well.

46
00:04:05,340 --> 00:04:06,170
Shut up and keep walking.

47
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:10,590
Did you hear what they said?

48
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:12,830
That's why I didn't want her
to take up wrestling.

49
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:13,880
You never listened!

50
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:16,589
You're scolding me as if I'm Aamir Khan
from Dangal

51
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:19,709
and she excelled because of my training.

52
00:04:19,790 --> 00:04:20,709
It's all because of you!

53
00:04:20,790 --> 00:04:22,500
You took her along
to every match you played.

54
00:04:22,590 --> 00:04:24,010
That's what inspired her to play.

55
00:04:24,090 --> 00:04:25,300
Why do you think I took her along?

56
00:04:25,380 --> 00:04:26,760
If I got hurt, 

57
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:29,170
I needed someone to inform my family.

58
00:04:29,290 --> 00:04:31,170
That's why I took her along.
How'd I know--

59
00:04:31,250 --> 00:04:32,170
Enough!

60
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:34,120
Many suitors visited.

61
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:35,300
Nothing seems to work out.

62
00:04:35,630 --> 00:04:37,090
Brother, don't worry.

63
00:04:37,170 --> 00:04:38,880
It's my responsibility
to get Keerthi married.

64
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,330
Hopeless! You're old and single!

65
00:04:41,630 --> 00:04:43,340
And you expect me to believe you.

66
00:04:45,250 --> 00:04:48,250
I'm afraid she will never get married.

67
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:49,470
Just the thought of it…

68
00:04:49,590 --> 00:04:50,470
Brother!

69
00:04:50,670 --> 00:04:51,550
Dad!

70
00:04:51,630 --> 00:04:52,550
Brother!

71
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:00,800
Doctor, how is he now?

72
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:03,300
Mrs. Sarojini, your husband, 
suffered a second attack.

73
00:05:03,630 --> 00:05:05,550
But he is out of danger now.

74
00:05:05,630 --> 00:05:06,710
Nothing to worry about.

75
00:05:06,790 --> 00:05:08,250
He will be under observation
for two days.

76
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:10,220
Keep him away from stress.

77
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:14,540
I'm why everyone is sad sitting

78
00:05:15,090 --> 00:05:16,420
at the hospital.

79
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,750
My love for wrestling is the reason.

80
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:20,760
How do I say this?

81
00:05:21,340 --> 00:05:23,260
It's an eighteen-year-old story.

82
00:05:23,590 --> 00:05:25,300
Keerthi was six at that time.

83
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:27,590
When I used to ask her
if she was dad or mom's pet, 

84
00:05:27,670 --> 00:05:29,880
she'd reply, "I'm uncle's pet."

85
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,790
Such was our bonding.

86
00:05:32,250 --> 00:05:34,540
I used to take her to school.

87
00:05:34,630 --> 00:05:36,760
-I used to feed and put her to bed.
-Bye, uncle.

88
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:38,620
She'd always be with me.

89
00:05:40,790 --> 00:05:41,870
During that time, 

90
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:43,340
a wrestling coach arrived.

91
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:45,420
I thought wrestling was easy

92
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:47,130
-and joined the class.
-Stop.

93
00:05:47,250 --> 00:05:50,420
But my tummy did get
in the way of my desire.

94
00:05:50,710 --> 00:05:51,920
Hey!

95
00:05:52,250 --> 00:05:54,330
After seeing me perform in a fight, 

96
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:56,790
the coach spoke to me.

97
00:05:57,210 --> 00:05:59,210
You can't wrestle
if your life depended on it!

98
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:01,830
-You're not fit for wrestling.
-Oh, no!

99
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:04,000
For God's sake, please find another hobby.

100
00:06:04,090 --> 00:06:05,010
Coach!

101
00:06:07,340 --> 00:06:10,630
Even if the world tells you you've lost, 

102
00:06:10,710 --> 00:06:14,130
you don't lose until you believe so.

103
00:06:14,210 --> 00:06:16,710
Still, I continued to lose.

104
00:06:16,790 --> 00:06:19,870
My defeat used to upset Keerthi.

105
00:06:20,790 --> 00:06:23,040
Uncle, why did you loosen your leg

106
00:06:23,170 --> 00:06:26,340
when that man locked your neck?

107
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,460
You could've tripped him

108
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:30,710
by applying the entire weight on his leg.

109
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:32,620
Why did I not think of it?

110
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:34,920
Tell me, how do you know about it?

111
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:36,960
Keerthi hoped that I should

112
00:06:37,090 --> 00:06:38,550
at least win a match.

113
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:41,880
Until the end, it remained a dream.

114
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:43,540
Bye!

115
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:45,090
Come on, raid!

116
00:06:45,420 --> 00:06:47,380
I was not good at wrestling.

117
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:50,250
But Keerthi, 
who grew up watching me was well-versed.

118
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:51,340
Yes!

119
00:06:51,590 --> 00:06:54,050
She participated in wrestling held
at school and won.

120
00:06:54,250 --> 00:06:55,830
It felt like I won.

121
00:06:57,670 --> 00:06:59,340
Keerthi joined college.

122
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:01,590
I hoped she would study in college.

123
00:07:01,790 --> 00:07:03,080
But she was determined

124
00:07:03,210 --> 00:07:04,880
and continued to wrestle.

125
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:24,130
Wrestling is a men's sport.

126
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:25,170
It won't suit you.

127
00:07:25,290 --> 00:07:27,080
Sport does not have a gender.

128
00:07:27,170 --> 00:07:29,130
If you check out the playground, 
everything is a sport.

129
00:07:29,210 --> 00:07:31,920
What if your face gets damaged wrestling?

130
00:07:32,290 --> 00:07:33,500
No one would marry you.

131
00:07:33,590 --> 00:07:34,970
My brother was determined

132
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:37,000
to get Keerthi married.

133
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:43,540
Is your daughter a wrestler?

134
00:07:43,750 --> 00:07:46,380
No… She used to do it in college.

135
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:49,040
-The short hair makes her look like a guy.
-Yes.

136
00:07:49,250 --> 00:07:50,920
A hundred sovereigns gold, 

137
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:52,540
ten lakh cash, and an Innova car.

138
00:07:52,750 --> 00:07:54,920
If this is fine with you, 
we'll take this further.

139
00:07:57,090 --> 00:07:58,760
It's an insult to me as a woman

140
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:00,220
to get married by offering a dowry.

141
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:01,630
You may please leave.

142
00:08:02,290 --> 00:08:03,790
Eve teasing got added

143
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:05,800
to the list of wrestling and dowry.

144
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,790
A few boys
at college harassed her sister, Raji.

145
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,330
She beat the hell out of them.

146
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:27,550
SREE NEELAKANTA GOVERNMENT
SAMSKRITHA COLLEGE, PATTAMBI

147
00:08:28,130 --> 00:08:29,090
Hey, run!

148
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:37,419
How dare you harass women?

149
00:08:40,710 --> 00:08:41,590
Oh, God!

150
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:53,010
The video of Keerthi thrashing the boys
at the bus stand

151
00:08:53,130 --> 00:08:55,760
went viral on social media and WhatsApp.

152
00:08:57,750 --> 00:08:58,960
Hereafter, no one from Kerala

153
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:01,000
will ask for your daughter's hand
in marriage.

154
00:09:01,250 --> 00:09:02,420
If you still insist, we will check

155
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:03,960
for suitors in another state.

156
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:05,380
God help us!

157
00:09:07,170 --> 00:09:08,800
It would have been a surprise

158
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:11,590
if my brother hadn't got a stroke
after all this chaos.

159
00:09:15,130 --> 00:09:16,010
Dad!

160
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,290
What did the doctor say?

161
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,540
Did he say I'll die sooner?

162
00:09:24,170 --> 00:09:25,090
Dad.

163
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:27,960
I'm not worried that I'm going to die.

164
00:09:28,630 --> 00:09:30,960
I'll die at peace

165
00:09:31,750 --> 00:09:33,290
if I see you get married.

166
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,630
For the women of our country, 

167
00:09:38,790 --> 00:09:40,460
family comes first.

168
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:43,750
Dreams and ambition come

169
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,340
after everything else.

170
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:47,460
Dad. Dad…

171
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:51,790
I can make it big as a wrestler.

172
00:09:53,040 --> 00:09:54,120
Trust me.

173
00:09:54,460 --> 00:09:56,250
We are middle-class people.

174
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:57,960
It won't suit us.

175
00:09:58,590 --> 00:10:00,630
Don't forget you have a younger sister.

176
00:10:01,130 --> 00:10:02,960
You must think about her life as well.

177
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:05,590
Please give up wrestling.

178
00:10:14,460 --> 00:10:15,880
Why are you crying?

179
00:10:16,710 --> 00:10:19,250
Is it because your father
asked you to give up wrestling?

180
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:21,920
He asked you not
to take part in a competition.

181
00:10:22,090 --> 00:10:23,590
Get married and continue

182
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:25,460
to wrestle inside your house.

183
00:10:27,290 --> 00:10:28,290
Confused?

184
00:10:29,590 --> 00:10:34,220
Every married woman is a wrestler.

185
00:10:34,590 --> 00:10:39,260
Every day, women have
to wrestle with their husbands.

186
00:10:41,670 --> 00:10:43,500
Did you wrestle with Grandpa?

187
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,130
Of course, I did!

188
00:10:45,420 --> 00:10:50,550
He got it well from me, 
and now he's resting in peace.

189
00:10:50,790 --> 00:10:51,750
Poor soul!

190
00:10:52,670 --> 00:10:55,670
Similarly, you will find a man

191
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,170
who'd wrestle with you for life.

192
00:11:05,170 --> 00:11:07,170
Veera! Veera!

193
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:09,800
Dude, go on a raid. Slay them all!

194
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Don't spare anyone!

195
00:11:12,130 --> 00:11:14,420
Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

196
00:11:16,750 --> 00:11:17,830
-Come on!
-Come!

197
00:11:18,250 --> 00:11:20,210
Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

198
00:11:20,790 --> 00:11:21,710
Veera!

199
00:11:22,460 --> 00:11:23,790
Kabaddi!

200
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:25,540
Veera!

201
00:11:26,590 --> 00:11:27,970
Kabaddi!

202
00:11:28,790 --> 00:11:29,830
Veera!

203
00:11:33,420 --> 00:11:34,300
Yeh!

204
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:38,130
We may arrive torpidly
If we stare, it will be ablaze

205
00:11:38,290 --> 00:11:41,330
When it dawns
We will create a fuss

206
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:45,000
Collars up
Coolers on

207
00:11:45,130 --> 00:11:48,300
The guy is handsome
The girl is beautiful

208
00:11:55,090 --> 00:11:58,090
We are playful at sight
But our grit is might

209
00:11:58,460 --> 00:12:01,790
Take a new route
Dance, thagida thagida thagida

210
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:05,170
This town is our fort
That bears my mighty picture

211
00:12:05,380 --> 00:12:08,760
I worked my charm
You fell for it

212
00:12:09,250 --> 00:12:10,130
Veera!

213
00:12:10,750 --> 00:12:11,630
Has arrived!

214
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:13,420
Veera!

215
00:12:31,590 --> 00:12:32,510
How is she?

216
00:12:32,630 --> 00:12:33,630
Please, turn around.

217
00:12:39,790 --> 00:12:43,000
In a street of coconut trees
We are the toddy shops

218
00:12:43,380 --> 00:12:46,460
We are the men
Who swim around pretty trouts

219
00:12:46,540 --> 00:12:49,420
-Hey, wearing garland
-We sear like crackers

220
00:12:49,710 --> 00:12:52,960
-If we come with trust
-We will take care of you

221
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:56,300
Hey guys, deal the cards
Let's play during the day

222
00:12:56,790 --> 00:12:58,170
Where are we going to study?

223
00:12:58,250 --> 00:13:00,130
We are always after fun
And create problems

224
00:13:00,210 --> 00:13:03,500
Beautiful like a bud
About the right size

225
00:13:03,670 --> 00:13:06,750
A new bindi on the forehead
She is a yellow angel

226
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:10,550
We may arrive torpidly
If we stare, it will be ablaze

227
00:13:10,670 --> 00:13:13,880
When it dawns
We will create a fuss

228
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:17,580
Collars up
Coolers on

229
00:13:17,710 --> 00:13:20,840
The guy is handsome
The girl is beautiful

230
00:13:22,710 --> 00:13:23,590
What about her?

231
00:13:23,750 --> 00:13:25,130
Wait. How far did she pursue her studies?

232
00:13:25,210 --> 00:13:26,670
She just graduated from ITI.

233
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,540
Such an educated girl won't suit me.

234
00:13:28,710 --> 00:13:30,210
I said ITI, not IIT.

235
00:13:30,590 --> 00:13:31,970
Even that is too much for me.

236
00:13:32,130 --> 00:13:33,380
I hope I'm making sense, Sattam.

237
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:37,750
We are playful at sight
But our grit is might

238
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:41,040
Take a new route
Dance, thagida thagida thagida

239
00:13:41,250 --> 00:13:44,330
This town is our fort
That bears my mighty picture

240
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:47,960
I worked my charm
You fell for it

241
00:14:05,460 --> 00:14:06,380
Please turn around.

242
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:08,920
You don't have to say anything.

243
00:14:17,670 --> 00:14:19,340
Hereafter don't take me
to find you a match.

244
00:14:20,170 --> 00:14:21,380
To hell with your preconditions.

245
00:14:21,590 --> 00:14:23,720
Hey, what's wrong with his preconditions?

246
00:14:24,090 --> 00:14:27,720
It's not wrong that he expects
his wife to be less educated than him.

247
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,960
He pursued it only till eighth grade.
That, too, he failed.

248
00:14:30,210 --> 00:14:31,750
In this age, it's hard
to find someone so less educated.

249
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:35,510
Thanks to COVID-19, 
everyone passed out of high school.

250
00:14:35,630 --> 00:14:37,590
We should look for a match ourselves.

251
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:39,130
How do you think I found my wife?

252
00:14:39,210 --> 00:14:41,210
Brother, how far is she educated?

253
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:42,960
She pursued it till fourth grade.

254
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:45,000
-How about you?
-Seventh grade!

255
00:14:45,210 --> 00:14:46,670
Listen, the Midday Meal Scheme

256
00:14:46,750 --> 00:14:48,880
was introduced to lure people like you.

257
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,250
Still, you didn't go to school.

258
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:52,330
Back in the day, passing seventh grade

259
00:14:52,460 --> 00:14:54,500
is considered as passing out MBBS today.

260
00:14:54,630 --> 00:14:56,010
Give me a scalpel. I'll perform surgery.

261
00:14:57,040 --> 00:15:00,170
Nothing would go wrong
if he married an educated girl.

262
00:15:01,090 --> 00:15:02,300
Sattam, an educated girl, 

263
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:04,080
will ask a hundred questions.

264
00:15:04,210 --> 00:15:07,130
But an uneducated girl will listen
to what I say.

265
00:15:07,380 --> 00:15:09,050
An educated girl will talk about
current affairs.

266
00:15:09,210 --> 00:15:10,340
An uneducated girl won't know

267
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:11,710
what's happening around her.

268
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:13,750
An educated girl will speak about

269
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:16,670
socialism, communism, and Periyarism.

270
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:18,960
But an uneducated girl will stick

271
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:21,420
to making curry and rasam for me.

272
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,420
To sum up, an uneducated girl
will abide by me.

273
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:26,420
Whereas I should
abide by an educated girl.

274
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:27,500
It's not just that.

275
00:15:27,750 --> 00:15:30,000
If the wife is less educated than you, 

276
00:15:30,090 --> 00:15:31,920
we can speak English as we please.

277
00:15:32,340 --> 00:15:33,300
Watch me now.

278
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,630
Hey, come here!

279
00:15:37,090 --> 00:15:38,670
One plate of fish fry.

280
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:40,920
Come on, hurry up!

281
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:43,710
How was it?

282
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:46,210
Brother, what you spoke is not English.

283
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:47,260
It's Hindi!

284
00:15:47,340 --> 00:15:49,220
Whether it is Hindi or English, 

285
00:15:49,540 --> 00:15:50,790
she is oblivious to it.

286
00:15:51,090 --> 00:15:52,510
I'm good as long as I get a fish fry.

287
00:15:53,130 --> 00:15:56,210
Okay, I can make peace with him
nit-picking about her studies.

288
00:15:56,790 --> 00:15:59,210
Why is he rejecting girls
because they have short hair?

289
00:16:00,420 --> 00:16:03,050
Listen, long hair is a beautiful asset
for women.

290
00:16:03,170 --> 00:16:04,590
With short hair, she's nothing but a man.

291
00:16:04,710 --> 00:16:07,130
Do you know what kind
of hair a girl should have?

292
00:16:07,380 --> 00:16:13,050
Long hair should run to her back
and hang above the ankles.

293
00:16:13,250 --> 00:16:14,580
When she walks, 

294
00:16:14,790 --> 00:16:17,460
it should oscillate like a pendulum.

295
00:16:17,670 --> 00:16:19,380
-What?
-I meant her hair.

296
00:16:19,670 --> 00:16:23,090
You see, the hair that flows in the air

297
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:26,050
should gracefully brush my face.

298
00:16:27,250 --> 00:16:30,080
When she lies next to me, 

299
00:16:30,170 --> 00:16:33,300
I want to embrace her hair.

300
00:16:33,790 --> 00:16:35,540
The fragrance of it…

301
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,630
A thick skull like you won't get it.

302
00:16:38,790 --> 00:16:42,710
There's another advantage to long hair.

303
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:45,800
If your wife speaks against you, 

304
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:52,880
you can swirl, hold, stamp, and beat her.

305
00:16:53,210 --> 00:16:55,380
She can neither run nor hide.

306
00:16:55,710 --> 00:16:58,880
Uncle, find me an obedient girl
like auntie.

307
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:00,580
Then you'd have to marry your aunt.

308
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:01,970
For kids from the 2000s, 

309
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:03,620
it's enough if it's a girl.

310
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:05,920
But you have remained single

311
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,420
with all your stupid preconditions.

312
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:09,710
Bloody 90s kids!

313
00:17:16,339 --> 00:17:18,010
Hey, are you going to puke?

314
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:20,960
-My wife is calling.
-Why is he scared of her?

315
00:17:21,089 --> 00:17:23,170
Uncle, he's such a weakling.

316
00:17:23,250 --> 00:17:24,250
THE LAW WILL DO ITS DUTY

317
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:34,840
-Son!
-Yeah!

318
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:37,210
I thought he was carrying law books
inside the backpack.

319
00:17:37,340 --> 00:17:39,130
But he's carrying a mini-saloon.

320
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:42,000
-Hopeless man!
-I'm taking my leave.

321
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:43,500
It's better not to drink

322
00:17:43,590 --> 00:17:44,840
than humiliate yourself.

323
00:17:45,130 --> 00:17:46,960
You'd realize when you get married.

324
00:17:47,130 --> 00:17:48,960
I'd remain the same even after marriage.

325
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:49,920
Wanna bet?

326
00:17:50,090 --> 00:17:53,130
I don't want to bet. Repeat what you said.

327
00:17:53,790 --> 00:17:55,460
I'd remain the same even after marriage.

328
00:17:55,590 --> 00:17:56,920
That's more like it!

329
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:57,920
This is enough.

330
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,630
-It'll be helpful in the future.
-Get lost!

331
00:17:59,750 --> 00:18:00,630
Get going!

332
00:18:00,750 --> 00:18:02,710
There's a council meeting in the morning.

333
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:04,500
Be present without fail.

334
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:07,250
Folks, how long should we wait?

335
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:08,420
Is Das coming or not?

336
00:18:08,670 --> 00:18:09,710
Someone, please find out.

337
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:34,670
I thought of building a factory, offering

338
00:18:34,750 --> 00:18:36,880
employment, and developing the village.

339
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:38,630
But you're against it like anti-Indians.

340
00:18:40,130 --> 00:18:41,550
What is your problem?

341
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:45,000
We're not against the idea of development.

342
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:47,130
But if the development is going to pollute

343
00:18:47,210 --> 00:18:49,500
the water, what do you expect?

344
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:51,550
The dye waste from your factory--

345
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:52,710
Old man, dye waste is obvious.

346
00:18:52,790 --> 00:18:54,120
What else do you expect?

347
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:57,380
Hey, stop joking!

348
00:18:57,710 --> 00:18:58,840
Wise men are talking.

349
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,750
I'll thrash you to dust.

350
00:19:00,920 --> 00:19:02,170
-Hey!
-To hell with you!

351
00:19:02,540 --> 00:19:03,460
Hey, Sattam!

352
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:08,420
Das, I hope you're aware four cows died

353
00:19:08,630 --> 00:19:10,670
after drinking the water from the pond.

354
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:12,380
Perhaps the cows died of disease.

355
00:19:12,590 --> 00:19:14,050
Why are you blaming it on me?

356
00:19:14,170 --> 00:19:16,380
More than half the village folks
drink water from that pond.

357
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:17,540
Everyone seems healthy.

358
00:19:17,670 --> 00:19:18,590
How do you know?

359
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,210
Go and check at the hospital.

360
00:19:20,630 --> 00:19:22,800
Every day many children get admitted
to the hospital.

361
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:24,670
It's not like they are all dead.

362
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:29,550
Sattam! He seems irrational.

363
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:31,550
-Let's shut down his factory.
-Sure!

364
00:19:31,630 --> 00:19:35,210
Look, you're the President
of this village, not India.

365
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:37,760
Das, curb your arrogance.

366
00:19:38,210 --> 00:19:40,840
Sattam, file a case.
We'll take him to court.

367
00:19:44,590 --> 00:19:47,220
To prove the charges against the accused, 

368
00:19:47,380 --> 00:19:49,300
the petitioner is granted one more month

369
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:50,880
to gather evidence.

370
00:19:51,210 --> 00:19:53,000
The court informed

371
00:19:53,210 --> 00:19:54,590
that until then, 

372
00:19:54,710 --> 00:19:57,790
there would be no stay put on the factory.

373
00:20:05,750 --> 00:20:07,210
Sattam, gather evidence

374
00:20:07,290 --> 00:20:08,790
and build a strong case.

375
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:09,800
Das is clever.

376
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:11,460
He would change the course of the case.

377
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:13,880
-We will be humiliated in court.
-I'll handle it.

378
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,250
Son. we're going to buy booze

379
00:20:15,340 --> 00:20:16,720
and then drive to the farm.

380
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:18,720
Uncle, 
today is mother's death anniversary.

381
00:20:18,840 --> 00:20:20,380
-So?
-You know that I don't drink on this day.

382
00:20:20,540 --> 00:20:21,670
I used to take money

383
00:20:21,750 --> 00:20:23,290
from your mother to drink.

384
00:20:23,590 --> 00:20:25,220
You didn't just take money
from his mother.

385
00:20:25,420 --> 00:20:26,750
You took money from his stepmother too.

386
00:20:27,170 --> 00:20:29,210
-You mean our stepmother?
-Yes!

387
00:20:32,710 --> 00:20:33,590
Hey!

388
00:20:33,710 --> 00:20:34,790
Hey! Watch out!

389
00:20:35,750 --> 00:20:36,630
Had you bumped me, 

390
00:20:36,750 --> 00:20:37,880
what would've happened?

391
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,420
I don't even have insurance.

392
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:41,170
Step out of the car. I said step out!

393
00:20:41,250 --> 00:20:44,080
It's the car that would get damaged
by bumping into you.

394
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:47,130
Hello, Mr. Big fat paunch!

395
00:20:47,670 --> 00:20:48,750
Hey, Ratnam!

396
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:51,460
-Wait, I'm coming.
-Come on!

397
00:20:51,630 --> 00:20:53,710
-Hey, how are you?
-I'm good!

398
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:56,620
What are you doing over here?

399
00:20:56,710 --> 00:20:59,000
I came to see my friend George.
He's an advocate over here.

400
00:20:59,090 --> 00:21:01,010
Oh, is it? This is my friend, Ganeshan.

401
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:03,090
We studied together till seventh grade.

402
00:21:03,750 --> 00:21:06,130
Your uncle studied
only till seventh grade.

403
00:21:06,340 --> 00:21:07,220
Showing off!

404
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:08,380
-Hop inside the car.
-Where to?

405
00:21:08,460 --> 00:21:10,500
-I need to talk to you.
-I have other work, dude.

406
00:21:18,090 --> 00:21:21,050
Ganesha, you used to look handsome
like Aravind Swami.

407
00:21:21,170 --> 00:21:22,500
What happened to you?

408
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:24,920
What to do? I have been busy.

409
00:21:25,130 --> 00:21:27,170
Come on.
You used to be handsome like Abbas.

410
00:21:27,340 --> 00:21:29,260
-But now you have changed.
-Did you hear that?

411
00:21:29,380 --> 00:21:30,710
I believe these two have never seen

412
00:21:30,790 --> 00:21:32,330
good-looking men in their lives.

413
00:21:32,670 --> 00:21:34,000
What are you whispering?

414
00:21:34,170 --> 00:21:35,750
Nothing, Mr. Handsome hunk, 
you carry on.

415
00:21:36,790 --> 00:21:39,290
Ratnam, you have a lavish life.

416
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:43,210
-Come on, it all belongs to my nephew.
-Oh, is it!

417
00:21:43,290 --> 00:21:45,540
Ratnam, is your nephew not drinking?

418
00:21:46,250 --> 00:21:48,330
-He does not drink.
-Nephew!

419
00:21:48,590 --> 00:21:51,550
-Why don't you have a drink?
-No thanks. You carry on.

420
00:21:51,670 --> 00:21:53,750
-What about a small one?
-No thanks.

421
00:21:53,840 --> 00:21:55,130
Don't force him.

422
00:21:55,210 --> 00:21:57,590
Such a great character, 
and that too in 2022.

423
00:21:58,670 --> 00:22:00,000
Is your nephew married?

424
00:22:00,130 --> 00:22:01,420
Not in this life!

425
00:22:02,250 --> 00:22:03,500
Are his stars maligned?

426
00:22:03,590 --> 00:22:04,630
Not just one

427
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:06,750
but all his stars are maligned.

428
00:22:08,540 --> 00:22:09,420
I don't get it!

429
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:18,340
I said ITI, not IIT.

430
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,580
I thinking
of getting Keerthi married to him.

431
00:22:22,790 --> 00:22:25,290
But their preconditions are hard to meet.

432
00:22:25,420 --> 00:22:26,670
Ganesha, seeing you think, 

433
00:22:26,790 --> 00:22:28,210
I believe you have a match for my nephew.

434
00:22:28,670 --> 00:22:29,750
He figured it out!

435
00:22:30,500 --> 00:22:31,380
Yes, there's a girl.

436
00:22:32,420 --> 00:22:34,630
-But she is not from here.
-Where's she from?

437
00:22:35,090 --> 00:22:35,970
Palakkad!

438
00:22:36,790 --> 00:22:39,170
-Palakkad, uh!
-Palakkad won't work out.

439
00:22:39,340 --> 00:22:41,130
It's not like
it's near the Pakistan border.

440
00:22:41,250 --> 00:22:42,540
It's near the Kerala border.

441
00:22:42,630 --> 00:22:44,670
-It's an hour's drive.
-Yeah!

442
00:22:44,750 --> 00:22:46,380
-Just 50 kilometers, nephew!
-Yes.

443
00:22:46,460 --> 00:22:48,540
Who is the girl? And how far
has she pursued her education?

444
00:22:48,790 --> 00:22:50,920
She is my niece.

445
00:22:51,290 --> 00:22:52,290
She studied till seventh grade.

446
00:22:53,040 --> 00:22:54,170
-Only till seventh grade?
-Yes.

447
00:22:54,250 --> 00:22:55,130
Why not more?

448
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:57,670
It's because you said
your nephew studied till eighth grade.

449
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:59,920
That's why I stopped after seventh grade.

450
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:05,880
Ganesha, how long is your niece's hair?

451
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:09,380
I said Kerala, and you're still in doubt.

452
00:23:09,540 --> 00:23:13,620
In India, only Kerala women
have the longest hair.

453
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:17,330
Their long hair will dance to their tunes.

454
00:23:17,460 --> 00:23:18,590
It has to be trimmed every month.

455
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:20,330
Why do you have to trim it every month?

456
00:23:20,460 --> 00:23:22,420
If they don't trim it, 
they will trip on it.

457
00:23:22,630 --> 00:23:23,920
Idiot, it'll get tangled.

458
00:23:24,170 --> 00:23:26,840
Ganesha, you better crash here tonight.

459
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:28,960
Tomorrow we'll go together
and see the girl.

460
00:23:29,090 --> 00:23:30,800
-Oh, God, no!
-What happened?

461
00:23:31,460 --> 00:23:34,170
You see, if you're coming to see my niece, 

462
00:23:34,250 --> 00:23:36,420
I need to make the necessary arrangements.

463
00:23:36,500 --> 00:23:37,960
If you show up unexpectedly, 

464
00:23:38,290 --> 00:23:39,750
my brother will get a stroke.

465
00:23:40,040 --> 00:23:41,370
Then there will be no wedding.

466
00:23:41,460 --> 00:23:43,210
Does your brother often get a stroke?

467
00:23:43,420 --> 00:23:45,250
Ratna, you wouldn't understand.

468
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:47,670
I have too much to do. I'm leaving!

469
00:23:47,750 --> 00:23:50,250
You bring your nephew to Palakkad.
We'll sort it out!

470
00:23:55,840 --> 00:23:57,170
I can't, and I won't!

471
00:23:57,250 --> 00:23:58,750
I can't wear this.

472
00:23:59,250 --> 00:24:00,580
Stop overreacting!

473
00:24:00,710 --> 00:24:02,340
It's not like women don't use it at all.

474
00:24:02,590 --> 00:24:05,010
I can't marry someone
who comes with terms and conditions.

475
00:24:05,250 --> 00:24:09,250
Every man has an expectation
of the woman, he's about to marry.

476
00:24:09,460 --> 00:24:12,790
Women, too, expect men to be

477
00:24:12,880 --> 00:24:16,380
well-settled in life before marriage.

478
00:24:16,790 --> 00:24:18,620
Mom, don't speak for the sake of it.

479
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:21,880
Don't you think he'll find out
if it's fake after marriage?

480
00:24:22,090 --> 00:24:23,260
It'll be humiliating!

481
00:24:23,500 --> 00:24:27,000
Dear, we can spew a thousand lies
to make a marriage.

482
00:24:27,170 --> 00:24:28,630
We are only going to lie about two things.

483
00:24:29,040 --> 00:24:30,420
Your education and your hair.

484
00:24:31,090 --> 00:24:32,010
Uncle!

485
00:24:32,090 --> 00:24:36,800
It's wrong to say
a high school pass-out is a graduate.

486
00:24:36,960 --> 00:24:41,840
You're a BSc graduate, but we will lie
and say you're a seventh-grade pass-out.

487
00:24:42,250 --> 00:24:43,210
This is not a lie

488
00:24:43,290 --> 00:24:45,000
because you did pass seventh grade.

489
00:24:45,790 --> 00:24:50,120
You won't find innocent guys
anywhere else but Tamil Nadu.

490
00:24:50,290 --> 00:24:54,790
Once you're married, 
everything will fall into place.

491
00:24:55,210 --> 00:24:56,130
She's right, dear!

492
00:24:56,340 --> 00:24:57,800
Please consider your father's condition.

493
00:24:58,630 --> 00:25:00,630
Sister, please say okay to it.

494
00:25:03,630 --> 00:25:04,800
Do as you please!

495
00:25:05,670 --> 00:25:06,550
My dear…

496
00:25:09,540 --> 00:25:10,460
-Success!
-Success!

497
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:18,420
How did I forget about this?

498
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:21,340
If they look at these pictures, 
we're doomed!

499
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:23,210
Here you go!

500
00:25:24,460 --> 00:25:26,420
Phew! Welcome son!

501
00:25:27,090 --> 00:25:29,670
-Welcome, everyone.
-Ganesha, I hope everything is ready.

502
00:25:29,750 --> 00:25:30,790
Perfectly ready!

503
00:25:30,880 --> 00:25:32,130
My brother won't get a stroke.

504
00:25:32,960 --> 00:25:34,710
-Greetings!
-Welcome!

505
00:25:36,170 --> 00:25:38,210
-All good?
-We are well!

506
00:25:38,710 --> 00:25:39,670
Sarojini!

507
00:26:01,670 --> 00:26:04,000
Son, be careful. You might spill.

508
00:26:26,540 --> 00:26:31,080
Dear, you look lovely with long hair.

509
00:26:32,250 --> 00:26:33,130
What?

510
00:26:33,210 --> 00:26:35,710
The old lady speaks
as if she's seeing her for the first time.

511
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:36,760
You're right.

512
00:26:37,090 --> 00:26:41,340
She recently got out of eye surgery.

513
00:26:41,500 --> 00:26:43,250
So, everything seems new to her.

514
00:26:44,170 --> 00:26:46,210
Mom, please stay silent for a while.

515
00:26:48,210 --> 00:26:50,670
I remember your daughter from somewhere…

516
00:26:51,170 --> 00:26:52,880
But I don't seem to place her.

517
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:55,630
Have you ever been to Palakkad before?

518
00:26:55,840 --> 00:26:56,720
I did not!

519
00:26:56,920 --> 00:26:58,800
Neither my daughter has visited Pollachi.

520
00:26:59,210 --> 00:27:00,540
Obviously, you did not meet her.

521
00:27:00,630 --> 00:27:02,340
I did not mean to say I met her in person.

522
00:27:02,460 --> 00:27:05,090
-But I feel I knew her--
-Hey, shut up!

523
00:27:06,670 --> 00:27:08,710
-What is your name?
-Keerthi.

524
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:11,080
How far are you educated?

525
00:27:12,540 --> 00:27:13,540
Seventh grade, right?

526
00:27:15,590 --> 00:27:17,010
Why do you ask him?

527
00:27:17,130 --> 00:27:18,170
It's you who studied.

528
00:27:18,250 --> 00:27:19,670
Agreed that she pursued education, 

529
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:22,000
-but it's he, who took her to the school.
-Yes, Ratnam.

