789
00:43:30,790 --> 00:43:32,000
What are you getting at?

790
00:43:32,540 --> 00:43:36,080
First three months after marriage
is a crucial period for husbands.

791
00:43:36,170 --> 00:43:39,800
The impression we make on our wives
will stay for life.

792
00:43:39,960 --> 00:43:41,840
She will think, my husband
is an important man in this village.

793
00:43:41,920 --> 00:43:43,380
Everyone looks up to him as a God.

794
00:43:43,630 --> 00:43:45,170
It's enough that I make her believe I'm

795
00:43:45,250 --> 00:43:47,130
the one to whom everyone comes for help.

796
00:43:47,250 --> 00:43:49,380
For life, she won't talk back to me.

797
00:43:50,170 --> 00:43:52,550
I'm sure your wife will be impressed!

798
00:43:53,000 --> 00:43:53,880
Not enough!

799
00:43:53,960 --> 00:43:56,000
We need to keep throwing a yorker

800
00:43:56,090 --> 00:43:57,590
to keep them in line.

801
00:44:05,170 --> 00:44:06,050
Hello!

802
00:44:06,130 --> 00:44:07,210
-Is sir home?
-Who are you?

803
00:44:07,290 --> 00:44:08,620
MLA wanted to speak to him.

804
00:44:08,840 --> 00:44:11,010
He's not home.
Shall I give you his mobile number?

805
00:44:11,170 --> 00:44:13,920
No, no! MLA will speak
to him only over the landline number.

806
00:44:14,880 --> 00:44:16,800
On the tenth, 
there's a textile showroom inauguration.

807
00:44:16,880 --> 00:44:18,090
Sir, has to cut the ribbon!

808
00:44:18,250 --> 00:44:19,580
Sure, I'll let him know.

809
00:44:20,090 --> 00:44:21,380
I know, sir is very busy.

810
00:44:21,460 --> 00:44:23,040
-Please make a note of the date.
-Okay.

811
00:44:24,130 --> 00:44:26,510
-Hello?
-Hello, I'm the Bank Manager.

812
00:44:27,090 --> 00:44:28,340
Mr. Rahul, speaking!

813
00:44:29,000 --> 00:44:30,290
I want to speak to Mr. Veera.

814
00:44:30,500 --> 00:44:31,460
Where is your husband?

815
00:44:31,710 --> 00:44:33,170
Hi, I'm Keerthi, his wife.

816
00:44:33,250 --> 00:44:34,580
He's not at home at this moment.

817
00:44:34,710 --> 00:44:36,670
I think he should return
in the next thirty minutes.

818
00:44:36,750 --> 00:44:39,210
But may I know what this is in regards to?

819
00:44:39,290 --> 00:44:41,670
-And which bank is it?
-Okay, finishing!

820
00:44:41,920 --> 00:44:42,880
Hello?

821
00:44:46,340 --> 00:44:48,010
I thought you said your wife
pursued education till seventh grade.

822
00:44:48,460 --> 00:44:49,420
Yes. Why do you ask?

823
00:44:49,540 --> 00:44:51,960
She didn't understand the English I spoke.

824
00:44:52,710 --> 00:44:54,880
It's enough.
Your wife might get scared.

825
00:44:55,960 --> 00:44:58,540
Huh. Just one more incident.

826
00:44:58,790 --> 00:45:00,750
I want to sweep her off her feet.

827
00:45:02,590 --> 00:45:04,670
Mani, a group, is loitering, holding

828
00:45:04,880 --> 00:45:06,590
these fliers, and asking for donations.

829
00:45:06,840 --> 00:45:08,590
Ask them to come home in the morning.

830
00:45:09,090 --> 00:45:10,010
Bye, Sattam.

831
00:45:10,420 --> 00:45:12,090
Hey, this is too much!

832
00:45:23,250 --> 00:45:24,380
-Madam!
-Madam!

833
00:45:24,500 --> 00:45:26,790
Hey! We're not beggars!

834
00:45:26,880 --> 00:45:28,510
We're here
to request a donation for the temple.

835
00:45:28,630 --> 00:45:30,050
And you guys are yearning like beggars.

836
00:45:30,130 --> 00:45:32,960
That is why people end up donating
chump change.

837
00:45:33,040 --> 00:45:34,080
Shut up and watch!

838
00:45:34,880 --> 00:45:36,050
Madam!

839
00:45:36,460 --> 00:45:37,540
Madam!

840
00:45:38,040 --> 00:45:39,920
-Who is it?
-Is, sir, home?

841
00:45:40,710 --> 00:45:42,040
He's in the shower. How can I help?

842
00:45:42,210 --> 00:45:43,590
This Friday, we're organizing a carnival

843
00:45:43,750 --> 00:45:45,080
at Uthukuli Deity temple.

844
00:45:45,500 --> 00:45:48,000
Please speak to your husband
and help us with a donation.

845
00:45:48,130 --> 00:45:49,880
Here you go.
Please show this to your husband.

846
00:45:50,130 --> 00:45:51,550
GRACIOUS DEITY AMMAN'S TEMPLE CARNIVAL

847
00:45:51,960 --> 00:45:53,960
Listen, people have come
asking for a donation.

848
00:45:54,460 --> 00:45:56,340
There is one lakh inside the desk drawer.

849
00:45:56,420 --> 00:45:57,340
Give it to them.

850
00:45:57,420 --> 00:45:58,880
-One lakh?
-Yes!

851
00:45:59,170 --> 00:46:00,920
Why would you donate such a large sum?

852
00:46:01,000 --> 00:46:02,540
Donations should be given
with an open heart.

853
00:46:02,710 --> 00:46:03,670
Do as I say!

854
00:46:06,710 --> 00:46:07,710
Here you go!

855
00:46:07,840 --> 00:46:09,920
Instead of money, 
you're bringing me an old newspaper.

856
00:46:10,040 --> 00:46:11,500
There is one lakh rupee inside it.

857
00:46:11,590 --> 00:46:12,590
One lakh?

858
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:15,960
She is not kidding.
It is one lakh rupees.

859
00:46:16,210 --> 00:46:17,460
Who is this philanthropist?

860
00:46:18,130 --> 00:46:19,010
My husband!

861
00:46:19,500 --> 00:46:22,290
Make sure you bring this great person
to the carnival.

862
00:46:22,380 --> 00:46:25,210
Hereafter, we will honor him
with all the titles.

863
00:46:25,670 --> 00:46:28,420
-Bye-bye. Goodbye, let's go!
-Thank you, madam!

864
00:46:40,880 --> 00:46:42,130
The judge is very strict.

865
00:46:42,710 --> 00:46:44,710
If they gather evidence against us, 

866
00:46:45,040 --> 00:46:46,750
it'll become tough to save the factory.

867
00:46:46,960 --> 00:46:49,710
I suggest you settle this matter
out of court.

868
00:46:53,710 --> 00:46:54,670
Don't you know how to cook?

869
00:46:54,790 --> 00:46:56,540
How could you not take away
the stones from the rice?

870
00:46:58,130 --> 00:46:59,380
Don't get worked up!

871
00:46:59,790 --> 00:47:01,500
Earlier, Veera was single.

872
00:47:01,670 --> 00:47:02,880
Now he is married.

873
00:47:02,960 --> 00:47:04,750
Why don't we kidnap his wife?

874
00:47:06,920 --> 00:47:08,000
Where is she from?

875
00:47:16,130 --> 00:47:17,130
I'm leaving.

876
00:47:22,130 --> 00:47:24,710
-Why is your hair all wet?
-I just took a bath.

877
00:47:24,960 --> 00:47:27,960
-I need to dry them.
-When? After you catch a cold?

878
00:47:28,960 --> 00:47:31,460
Come! Don't overthink, come!

879
00:47:35,920 --> 00:47:37,840
I have noticed that you never

880
00:47:37,920 --> 00:47:39,250
hair dry using benzoin.

881
00:47:39,540 --> 00:47:40,920
Didn't your mother teach you anything?

882
00:47:41,670 --> 00:47:43,050
It's not enough that you grow your hair.

883
00:47:43,130 --> 00:47:44,340
You have to maintain it.

884
00:47:44,670 --> 00:47:45,670
That's quintessential.

885
00:47:45,880 --> 00:47:47,300
If not, you'll start losing hair.

886
00:47:51,670 --> 00:47:53,670
-Hurry up, brother.
-Hold your horses. I'll be there.

887
00:48:07,460 --> 00:48:09,000
You draw a good rangoli.

888
00:48:17,210 --> 00:48:18,380
Hey, throw on the offside.

889
00:48:18,750 --> 00:48:20,250
Come on, throw to this side.

890
00:48:32,290 --> 00:48:33,460
Is this how you play?

891
00:48:33,590 --> 00:48:35,130
You spoiled my rangoli.

892
00:48:35,290 --> 00:48:37,080
Why did you draw a rangoli out here?

893
00:48:38,460 --> 00:48:40,670
Where else do you want me to
draw a rangoli?

894
00:48:41,040 --> 00:48:42,330
Go and play at your house.

895
00:48:42,420 --> 00:48:44,340
-Ball?
-I won't return your ball.

896
00:48:44,460 --> 00:48:46,210
Get lost! I said, get lost!

897
00:48:49,130 --> 00:48:50,380
Fooling around early in the morning.

898
00:49:01,590 --> 00:49:02,470
Hello!

899
00:49:02,630 --> 00:49:04,300
I'm bringing friends over for lunch.

900
00:49:04,460 --> 00:49:05,880
Hunt a rooster and make curry.

901
00:49:06,130 --> 00:49:08,130
I don't know how to make chicken curry.

902
00:49:09,290 --> 00:49:10,210
Hello?

903
00:49:10,840 --> 00:49:11,800
Hello?

904
00:49:21,840 --> 00:49:23,220
Hey, stop!

905
00:49:23,840 --> 00:49:24,800
I said, stop!

906
00:49:27,790 --> 00:49:29,790
Even if you climb up, 
I won't spare you.

907
00:49:32,040 --> 00:49:33,370
Hey, don't run!

908
00:49:42,590 --> 00:49:44,220
Hey, I got you!

909
00:49:55,130 --> 00:49:56,380
Are you trying to hunt a rooster?

910
00:49:57,710 --> 00:49:59,840
If we help you hunt, 
would you return the ball?

911
00:50:01,670 --> 00:50:03,590
-Hey, catch it.
-Don't let it go. Grab it!

912
00:50:03,710 --> 00:50:05,090
Guys, come around and catch it!

913
00:50:06,420 --> 00:50:08,840
-Come on, hurry up!
-Don't lose it!

914
00:50:09,040 --> 00:50:10,710
-Hurry up!
-Where the hell is it going?

915
00:50:10,920 --> 00:50:12,840
-Come on! Come on!
-It's on the tree.

916
00:50:12,920 --> 00:50:14,050
Shake the tree.

917
00:50:14,340 --> 00:50:16,130
-I will catch it.
-I will catch it!

918
00:50:16,290 --> 00:50:17,790
-I caught you!
-You're getting cooked today!

919
00:50:17,960 --> 00:50:20,000
-What now?
-Now put tomatoes.

920
00:50:20,130 --> 00:50:21,800
-Did you add them?
-Yes, I added tomatoes.

921
00:50:21,920 --> 00:50:22,880
What else?

922
00:50:24,130 --> 00:50:26,800
I added coriander, 
curry leaves, green chilies, 

923
00:50:26,880 --> 00:50:29,260
and finally, I added tomatoes too.

924
00:50:29,340 --> 00:50:30,800
-Is that enough?
-Now mix it and cook well.

925
00:50:30,880 --> 00:50:31,840
Okay, I'll take it from here.

926
00:50:32,340 --> 00:50:34,300
Sister, are you having guests over?

927
00:50:34,670 --> 00:50:35,550
No!

928
00:50:35,960 --> 00:50:37,590
Then why are you making so much food?

929
00:50:37,790 --> 00:50:40,080
My husband is bringing over
his friends for lunch.

930
00:50:40,250 --> 00:50:41,710
Are you cooking for
your husband's friends?

931
00:50:42,210 --> 00:50:43,090
Yes!

932
00:50:43,290 --> 00:50:45,460
We wouldn't have helped you hunt
if we had known about it earlier.

933
00:50:45,880 --> 00:50:46,960
Let's go!

934
00:50:47,460 --> 00:50:48,290
What happened?

935
00:50:48,380 --> 00:50:50,960
-It's because we don't get along well.
-It's because we don't get along well.

936
00:50:51,710 --> 00:50:53,380
Listen, you should not disrespect elders.

937
00:50:53,630 --> 00:50:55,590
Elders? They are all cheapskates.

938
00:50:55,960 --> 00:50:56,840
Are you guys serious?

939
00:50:57,130 --> 00:50:59,760
They will head out to the council
to resolve an issue.

940
00:50:59,880 --> 00:51:03,130
But they will blow the issue
out of proportion.

941
00:51:03,420 --> 00:51:05,550
Most of the time, 
the council meetings end in a fight.

942
00:51:05,790 --> 00:51:07,670
There are instances they got beaten up.

943
00:51:07,790 --> 00:51:09,500
Even now, they're playing kabaddi

944
00:51:09,590 --> 00:51:10,510
at the school playground.

945
00:51:10,710 --> 00:51:13,040
And you're here cooking
for those cheapskates.

946
00:51:17,710 --> 00:51:19,790
He asked you to cook
and didn't turn up for lunch.

947
00:51:20,170 --> 00:51:22,130
And you believed he'd come
and starve yourself.

948
00:51:23,040 --> 00:51:24,750
If we keep up the charade to eat

949
00:51:24,840 --> 00:51:26,840
only after the husband eats, 

950
00:51:26,960 --> 00:51:28,630
then for life, we'll be hungry.

951
00:51:28,750 --> 00:51:30,750
Husbands will find their meals
as they please.

952
00:51:30,880 --> 00:51:33,010
Your husband might be wealthy.

953
00:51:33,090 --> 00:51:35,260
But how long could he mooch off it?

954
00:51:35,460 --> 00:51:37,090
He has emptied most of his wealth.

955
00:51:37,290 --> 00:51:39,750
Now only this house and the farm are left.

956
00:51:39,880 --> 00:51:42,670
It's up to you to save whatever is left.

957
00:51:43,040 --> 00:51:46,250
-So--
-Veera grew up without his parents.

958
00:51:46,500 --> 00:51:47,880
His uncle is not a good guardian

959
00:51:48,040 --> 00:51:49,460
and did not raise him well.

960
00:51:49,540 --> 00:51:50,920
At least you stay patient with him

961
00:51:51,000 --> 00:51:52,000
and get him on track.

962
00:51:52,210 --> 00:51:53,880
For thirty years, they spoil their sons

963
00:51:54,090 --> 00:51:55,920
and get them married to us.

964
00:51:56,130 --> 00:51:58,050
And the mothers-in-law expect us

965
00:51:58,130 --> 00:51:59,510
to straighten them out.

966
00:51:59,960 --> 00:52:01,710
It's not our job to get them on track.

967
00:52:01,880 --> 00:52:03,800
It's not like we were born to do it.

968
00:52:04,380 --> 00:52:06,550
I wonder what mothers do

969
00:52:06,630 --> 00:52:08,630
with their sons for thirty years.

970
00:52:09,130 --> 00:52:10,510
He always hangs out with useless friends.

971
00:52:10,840 --> 00:52:12,840
No one is capable of anything.

972
00:52:13,000 --> 00:52:14,250
They drink to their necks.

973
00:52:14,340 --> 00:52:15,760
You say that no one has a job.

974
00:52:15,880 --> 00:52:17,960
-How do they get money to drink?
-Don't even ask!

975
00:52:18,210 --> 00:52:19,290
Even if they don't have money, 

976
00:52:19,420 --> 00:52:20,460
they'll borrow to drink.

977
00:52:25,170 --> 00:52:27,130
Brother, 
why do you not like your better half?

978
00:52:27,250 --> 00:52:28,170
Who said so?

979
00:52:28,500 --> 00:52:31,210
Every man likes a better half very much.

980
00:52:31,500 --> 00:52:33,540
But it has
to be another man's better half.

981
00:52:35,170 --> 00:52:36,960
In this world full of shapes, 

982
00:52:37,040 --> 00:52:38,830
these men are with no form.

983
00:52:39,000 --> 00:52:40,380
That's an apt description of these men.

984
00:52:40,500 --> 00:52:41,920
If we start taking a form

985
00:52:42,000 --> 00:52:43,330
the world can't take it.

986
00:52:43,500 --> 00:52:45,380
We live a life bound by truth.

987
00:52:45,670 --> 00:52:47,130
Men talk too much of themselves.

988
00:52:47,210 --> 00:52:49,170
Do you think they can bear the labor pain?

989
00:52:49,380 --> 00:52:50,420
They experience pain

990
00:52:50,500 --> 00:52:51,630
only when they're in labor.

991
00:52:51,880 --> 00:52:54,210
But we men struggle our entire lives

992
00:52:54,290 --> 00:52:55,790
to raise the child.

993
00:52:56,420 --> 00:52:58,550
-It's unimaginable…
-To heck with them!

994
00:52:58,670 --> 00:53:02,170
Try bathing and changing diapers.
Can they do it?

995
00:53:02,250 --> 00:53:03,630
Back then, my grandma

996
00:53:03,750 --> 00:53:05,420
had ten children, raised them, 

997
00:53:05,500 --> 00:53:07,210
and handled all the chores.

998
00:53:07,380 --> 00:53:08,880
At present, it's just one child, 

999
00:53:08,960 --> 00:53:10,540
and they expect us to help them.

1000
00:53:10,790 --> 00:53:13,870
Nowadays, there's a machine available
for every job.

1001
00:53:14,090 --> 00:53:15,550
Switching on machines is simple.

1002
00:53:15,630 --> 00:53:17,170
That is why I suggest, 

1003
00:53:17,290 --> 00:53:19,580
whether we men have a job or not, 

1004
00:53:19,750 --> 00:53:21,960
leave the house in the morning.

1005
00:53:22,130 --> 00:53:24,090
Once you leave in the morning, 

1006
00:53:24,170 --> 00:53:25,380
return only at night

1007
00:53:25,460 --> 00:53:26,790
after the soap operas.

1008
00:53:26,920 --> 00:53:28,460
That's the beauty of manhood!

1009
00:53:28,840 --> 00:53:31,720
They get well-dressed in the morning
and leave.

1010
00:53:31,840 --> 00:53:33,970
But they're unaware of
where they're headed.

1011
00:53:34,130 --> 00:53:36,010
We're the head of the family for namesake.

1012
00:53:36,090 --> 00:53:37,170
But we don't even get space

1013
00:53:37,290 --> 00:53:38,620
in the cupboard to keep our clothes.

1014
00:53:38,750 --> 00:53:40,830
Women buy sarees for every occasion

1015
00:53:40,960 --> 00:53:43,130
and pile them in the cupboard.

1016
00:53:43,340 --> 00:53:44,670
But they'd dress up

1017
00:53:44,750 --> 00:53:46,460
as if they have no clothes

1018
00:53:46,540 --> 00:53:49,370
and wear torn nighties all the time.

1019
00:53:49,460 --> 00:53:50,340
Damn!

1020
00:53:50,460 --> 00:53:52,540
Except for weddings, they wear nighties

1021
00:53:52,630 --> 00:53:54,630
to every place they visit.

1022
00:53:54,840 --> 00:53:56,470
They look like a
cylinder wrapped in cloth.

1023
00:53:56,670 --> 00:53:58,130
That's such a turn-off!

1024
00:53:58,420 --> 00:54:00,000
When we come home at night, 

1025
00:54:00,130 --> 00:54:02,130
if they receive us well-dressed in saree
and flowers, 

1026
00:54:02,290 --> 00:54:03,620
we will get enticed.

1027
00:54:03,710 --> 00:54:05,790
-Rightly said!
-No wonder our ancestors had many kids.

1028
00:54:06,090 --> 00:54:07,090
Sarees are the leading cause.

1029
00:54:07,170 --> 00:54:10,050
The saree is the sexiest attire
in the world.

1030
00:54:10,130 --> 00:54:11,510
But the women don't wear them.

1031
00:54:11,590 --> 00:54:12,880
Why can't they wear a saree?

1032
00:54:12,960 --> 00:54:15,710
As if we wear a saree, 
they'd ravish us.

1033
00:54:16,170 --> 00:54:17,710
Only I know the struggle

1034
00:54:17,790 --> 00:54:19,370
I went through to have a child.

1035
00:54:19,500 --> 00:54:21,330
For these men, 
the nighties are more than enough.

1036
00:54:21,710 --> 00:54:24,540
You should glare at your wife
for no reason.

1037
00:54:24,880 --> 00:54:26,380
If they mildly glare at us, 

1038
00:54:26,500 --> 00:54:28,000
we should sternly glare at them.

1039
00:54:28,500 --> 00:54:33,000
Call them out and give them a tight slap, 
even if you don't find a reason.

1040
00:54:33,170 --> 00:54:34,460
If they land one slap, 

1041
00:54:34,540 --> 00:54:36,290
we should return it with two tight slaps.

1042
00:54:36,670 --> 00:54:40,880
You see, we can't straighten our wives
with love.

1043
00:54:41,460 --> 00:54:42,670
Only violence works.

1044
00:54:42,750 --> 00:54:45,710
Husbands can't be straightened
with sentiments.

1045
00:54:45,840 --> 00:54:47,340
We need to whack the hell out of them!

1046
00:54:47,960 --> 00:54:48,920
Come on, ladies, let's go.

1047
00:54:49,000 --> 00:54:51,710
Your husband's uncle is the root cause
of all your problems.

1048
00:54:51,880 --> 00:54:54,510
Make sure your husband does not
hang out with him.

1049
00:54:55,040 --> 00:54:56,250
-Nephew!
-Yeah!

1050
00:54:56,540 --> 00:54:58,000
-Give me your phone.
-Why?

1051
00:54:58,170 --> 00:54:59,590
Let us call your wife.

1052
00:54:59,670 --> 00:55:01,670
-Here, talk to her.
-What do I say?

1053
00:55:02,000 --> 00:55:04,500
Ask her to reheat the chicken curry

1054
00:55:04,670 --> 00:55:06,800
and make fluffy rice cakes.

1055
00:55:06,960 --> 00:55:10,590
They will be ready
and hot to serve by the time you reach.

1056
00:55:10,670 --> 00:55:12,250
-She did not pick up.
-The rice cakes?

1057
00:55:12,420 --> 00:55:15,590
-She did not take my call.
-Hey, stop! Stop, I say!

1058
00:55:15,840 --> 00:55:17,760
-Stop!
-Why did you ask me to stop?

1059
00:55:18,000 --> 00:55:20,960
I told you a million times
not to be romantic with your wife.

1060
00:55:21,040 --> 00:55:22,580
And handle her sternly.
You never listened.

1061
00:55:22,670 --> 00:55:23,920
I'm strict with her!

1062
00:55:24,040 --> 00:55:25,870
If you were strict, 
she would've taken your call.

1063
00:55:27,130 --> 00:55:28,050
You call her again.

1064
00:55:28,960 --> 00:55:32,500
A wife should pick up at the first ring
when the husband calls.

1065
00:55:32,630 --> 00:55:34,090
She let it ring all the way.

1066
00:55:34,170 --> 00:55:35,590
That means she does not respect you.

1067
00:55:36,420 --> 00:55:37,800
Uncle, you misunderstood her.

1068
00:55:37,880 --> 00:55:39,130
I'm telling the truth.

1069
00:55:39,210 --> 00:55:41,380
Get home right now
and get your wife under control.

1070
00:55:41,590 --> 00:55:42,920
If not, it will ruin your life, 

1071
00:55:43,000 --> 00:55:44,420
just like butcher Murugesan.

1072
00:55:45,340 --> 00:55:47,590
-Give it to me.
-Hey, you forgot about me!

1073
00:55:47,670 --> 00:55:48,920
Hey, I did not get on the bike.

1074
00:55:54,840 --> 00:55:55,720
Keerthi!

1075
00:55:57,540 --> 00:55:58,460
Keerthi!

1076
00:55:59,880 --> 00:56:00,760
Keerthi!

1077
00:56:01,790 --> 00:56:02,670
Open the door!

1078
00:56:03,710 --> 00:56:04,630
I ought to!

1079
00:56:16,880 --> 00:56:19,340
Why did you come through
the back entrance?

1080
00:56:21,250 --> 00:56:23,210
I wouldn't have come through
the back entrance

1081
00:56:23,290 --> 00:56:25,120
had you answered the door.

1082
00:56:25,210 --> 00:56:28,340
Oh, it was late, and I dozed off.

1083
00:56:28,460 --> 00:56:30,000
Let me serve you food.

1084
00:56:35,420 --> 00:56:36,960
Uncle was right about her.

1085
00:56:37,710 --> 00:56:39,590
I have to handle her differently.

1086
00:56:40,250 --> 00:56:41,500
Please come and eat.

1087
00:56:42,250 --> 00:56:43,830
-What is this?
-Food!

1088
00:56:44,130 --> 00:56:46,210
It's not fresh food but leftovers.

1089
00:56:46,840 --> 00:56:48,800
Have you heard someone eating leftovers

1090
00:56:48,880 --> 00:56:50,130
after being drunk?

1091
00:56:50,500 --> 00:56:51,460
Are you drunk?

1092
00:56:53,090 --> 00:56:54,920
When the husband is late, 

1093
00:56:55,040 --> 00:56:56,620
it means he'll come home drunk.

1094
00:56:57,040 --> 00:56:58,580
The wife should not question him.

1095
00:56:58,750 --> 00:57:01,500
Oh, then, who else do you expect
to question you?

1096
00:57:03,040 --> 00:57:05,830
It's not the husband's duty
to answer the wife.

1097
00:57:06,090 --> 00:57:09,340
How do you expect me to do my job
If I keep answering you all day?

1098
00:57:09,670 --> 00:57:10,710
What other job do you have?

1099
00:57:10,920 --> 00:57:12,380
What other job?

1100
00:57:13,750 --> 00:57:15,420
Do you even know what a husband does?

1101
00:57:15,540 --> 00:57:19,290
In a day, he meets many people, 

1102
00:57:19,380 --> 00:57:22,010
manages people, 
and gets into a lot of fights.

1103
00:57:22,460 --> 00:57:25,090
Every day is like a war for men.

1104
00:57:25,500 --> 00:57:29,670
Rightfully, when the husband returns
from the war, 

1105
00:57:30,040 --> 00:57:35,080
the wife has to pray and honor him.

1106
00:57:36,170 --> 00:57:37,710
Does this apply to the husbands

1107
00:57:37,790 --> 00:57:39,330
who loiter the entire day too?

1108
00:57:39,840 --> 00:57:41,010
Loitering?

1109
00:57:41,090 --> 00:57:44,630
I am well aware of you and your gang.

1110
00:57:47,340 --> 00:57:48,340
Everything, as in?

1111
00:57:49,040 --> 00:57:50,330
Everything, as in everything.

1112
00:57:53,340 --> 00:57:54,260
How?

1113
00:57:54,840 --> 00:57:55,670
I got to know.

1114
00:57:56,460 --> 00:57:57,420
Oh!

1115
00:58:10,750 --> 00:58:14,170
Oh, so you have assigned a pie.

1116
00:58:14,540 --> 00:58:15,460
Pie?

1117
00:58:15,540 --> 00:58:17,540
To hire someone to check

1118
00:58:17,670 --> 00:58:20,500
on your husband's activities.

1119
00:58:21,380 --> 00:58:22,550
Oh, you meant spy!

1120
00:58:23,340 --> 00:58:27,800
Listen, whatever you heard about me
is what I am.

1121
00:58:28,670 --> 00:58:31,500
It's better you come to terms with
and be a homemaker.

1122
00:58:31,790 --> 00:58:35,580
Instead, if you dare question me
unnecessarily…

1123
00:58:38,920 --> 00:58:39,920
Don't you glare!

1124
00:58:41,130 --> 00:58:43,710
Many beat up their wives for no reason.

1125
00:58:43,920 --> 00:58:48,050
But I'm particular that I will beat
only with a reason.

1126
00:58:49,210 --> 00:58:51,000
Don't make me do it!

1127
00:58:53,670 --> 00:58:54,750
Don't mess with me!

1128
00:59:05,840 --> 00:59:06,840
What was the case?

1129
00:59:06,960 --> 00:59:07,920
To excavate the pond

1130
00:59:08,040 --> 00:59:09,370
the Government allotted fifteen lakhs.

1131
00:59:09,540 --> 00:59:10,870
-Okay!
-There's a complaint

1132
00:59:11,000 --> 00:59:12,960
against you to have misused the money.

1133
00:59:13,210 --> 00:59:16,170
Hey, the fund is yet to be sanctioned.

1134
00:59:16,340 --> 00:59:17,550
And you come here saying

1135
00:59:17,630 --> 00:59:19,130
I misused the money. Are you serious?

1136
00:59:19,380 --> 00:59:20,960
The clerk said it got sanctioned

1137
00:59:21,040 --> 00:59:22,750
last month, and you signed.

1138
00:59:23,250 --> 00:59:24,540
He has stated the same.

1139
00:59:24,630 --> 00:59:26,090
Uncle, what is the problem?

1140
00:59:26,210 --> 00:59:28,540
Someone is conspiring against us.

1141
00:59:28,840 --> 00:59:29,720
Who is it?

1142
00:59:29,920 --> 00:59:32,380
When you stand up for the people, 
they stop the honest men

1143
00:59:32,460 --> 00:59:33,590
and let go of the dishonest ones.

1144
00:59:33,670 --> 00:59:35,800
You speak to Sattam
and arrange for my bail.

1145
00:59:35,880 --> 00:59:36,710
Let's go!

1146
00:59:46,500 --> 00:59:49,170
She's really raring to go now…

1147
00:59:49,750 --> 00:59:50,710
How well are they gonna…

1148
01:00:11,380 --> 01:00:12,510
Where is your husband?

1149
01:00:13,880 --> 01:00:15,210
He's not home.

1150
01:00:16,290 --> 01:00:20,420
Why is he not home
when his newlywed wife sits at home?

1151
01:00:20,630 --> 01:00:21,920
She may look slim.

1152
01:00:22,000 --> 01:00:23,790
Still, she seems voluptuous.

1153
01:00:24,290 --> 01:00:26,210
Are there no men in Kerala to marry?

1154
01:00:26,290 --> 01:00:27,580
Why did you get married to him?

1155
01:00:27,750 --> 01:00:29,920
Oh, so she's from Kerala!

1156
01:00:30,040 --> 01:00:33,330
I watched Malena five times.

1157
01:00:33,540 --> 01:00:36,420
It's still fresh in my mind.
Have you watched it?

1158
01:00:36,500 --> 01:00:38,380
I'm sure she's seen it.

1159
01:00:45,250 --> 01:00:46,210
Listen.

1160
01:00:47,000 --> 01:00:49,130
I spent millions on this factory.

1161
01:00:49,790 --> 01:00:52,420
Your husband and the President
have filed a case to shut it down.

1162
01:00:52,670 --> 01:00:54,380
Why do they have to interfere
in my matters?

1163
01:00:54,540 --> 01:00:57,580
I got the President arrested
so that he does not attend the hearing.

1164
01:00:58,000 --> 01:00:59,960
Now I have to take care of your husband.

1165
01:01:00,210 --> 01:01:02,210
Make sure he does not come to court.

1166
01:01:03,960 --> 01:01:05,420
If he still makes it to the court, 

1167
01:01:05,750 --> 01:01:08,500
then you'll have to find another husband.

1168
01:01:09,170 --> 01:01:10,300
I have many options for you.

1169
01:01:11,250 --> 01:01:12,330
Don't worry about it.

1170
01:01:12,750 --> 01:01:14,130
-What do you guys say?
-We are here!

1171
01:01:15,380 --> 01:01:16,340
See, they're eager!

1172
01:01:48,290 --> 01:01:49,370
How did it break?

1173
01:01:53,000 --> 01:01:54,460
I asked how did it break?

1174
01:01:55,210 --> 01:01:57,000
The factory owner came with his men
and threatened me.

1175
01:01:57,630 --> 01:01:59,300
Oh, Das came?

1176
01:01:59,880 --> 01:02:02,210
-What did he say?
-He asked you not to come to the court.

1177
01:02:02,380 --> 01:02:03,630
If I go, what would he do?

1178
01:02:04,000 --> 01:02:05,540
He can't do anything to me.

1179
01:02:05,790 --> 01:02:08,040
Here, he can only break this remote.

1180
01:02:08,790 --> 01:02:10,500
When the man of the house isn't home, 

1181
01:02:10,840 --> 01:02:13,300
he shows his prowess to the women.

1182
01:02:13,840 --> 01:02:15,010
Once the court gives its verdict…

1183
01:02:15,790 --> 01:02:16,790
I'll handle him!

1184
01:02:16,880 --> 01:02:18,760
Listen, you don't have
to be afraid of him.

1185
01:02:18,840 --> 01:02:19,970
It's very common here.

1186
01:02:20,420 --> 01:02:22,590
You may have been a scared Malayali girl.

1187
01:02:22,920 --> 01:02:25,130
But now you should be
a courageous Thamizh girl.

1188
01:02:25,630 --> 01:02:26,550
Understood?

1189
01:02:27,840 --> 01:02:28,970
Do you understand?

1190
01:02:30,290 --> 01:02:31,170
Understood!

1191
01:02:38,840 --> 01:02:39,800
In this case, 

1192
01:02:39,920 --> 01:02:43,340
based on the evidence presented
by the petitioner, 

1193
01:02:43,710 --> 01:02:47,630
it's confirmed that the industrial wastage
from the factory

1194
01:02:47,710 --> 01:02:50,170
gets mixed with lake water

1195
01:02:50,290 --> 01:02:52,920
and has affected people's health.

1196
01:02:53,210 --> 01:02:58,500
Therefore, this court orders
the Kovai Collector

1197
01:02:58,670 --> 01:03:02,090
to shut down the factory immediately.

1198
01:03:05,340 --> 01:03:06,920
TRUTH ALONE TRIUMPHS

1199
01:03:07,170 --> 01:03:08,170
Awesome!

1200
01:03:09,000 --> 01:03:09,880
That's great!

1201
01:03:50,130 --> 01:03:52,170
Welcome, Mr. Philanthropist!

1202
01:03:52,250 --> 01:03:53,750
Please come, we're waiting.

1203
01:03:57,920 --> 01:03:59,800
-Are you from the event committee?
-Yes! Why do you ask?

1204
01:03:59,880 --> 01:04:03,300
To show off to my wife, 
I donated a large sum.

1205
01:04:03,380 --> 01:04:04,550
At least return half of the amount.

1206
01:04:05,040 --> 01:04:07,080
Hey, I'm running short on funds.
Please return it.

1207
01:04:07,210 --> 01:04:09,210
Hey, speak like a philanthropist.

1208
01:04:09,460 --> 01:04:11,090
Look, I spent a lot.

1209
01:04:11,290 --> 01:04:12,960
They will give you sweets after prayers.

1210
01:04:13,040 --> 01:04:14,250
Be happy with what you get.

1211
01:04:14,380 --> 01:04:16,260
Put on the garland. Start the music.

1212
01:04:29,210 --> 01:04:30,130
Hello!

1213
01:04:30,960 --> 01:04:31,920
Hello, who is this?

1214
01:04:32,340 --> 01:04:34,050
One minute. Hold this. I'll be back.

1215
01:04:35,290 --> 01:04:36,960
Hello? Hold on!

1216
01:04:37,250 --> 01:04:39,330
Hello? Hello? I can't hear anything.

1217
01:04:40,170 --> 01:04:41,420
Yeah, speak now, 

1218
01:04:43,960 --> 01:04:46,420
Senthil? There's no one by that name.

1219
01:06:26,460 --> 01:06:28,380
Is building a factory an easy task?

1220
01:06:28,750 --> 01:06:30,420
Do you know it's a huge process?

1221
01:06:30,500 --> 01:06:32,500
You filed a petty case and shut it down.

1222
01:06:33,130 --> 01:06:34,300
Bear this in mind.

1223
01:06:34,540 --> 01:06:37,000
I can splurge money and reinstate
my factory tomorrow.

1224
01:06:37,540 --> 01:06:38,500
But I won't do it!

1225
01:06:38,750 --> 01:06:40,420
Only if I kill you in front of everyone

1226
01:06:40,500 --> 01:06:42,250
no one will dare mess with me again.

1227
01:06:42,340 --> 01:06:43,220
Hey!

1228
01:06:45,710 --> 01:06:46,710
Give it to me!

1229
01:07:20,880 --> 01:07:23,210
How dare you lay your hands on our boss?
I ought to--

1230
01:07:55,000 --> 01:07:56,000
She's valorous!

1231
01:07:59,840 --> 01:08:00,840
She's valorous!

1232
01:08:22,960 --> 01:08:24,920
Hey, you brought your wife to fight.

1233
01:08:25,040 --> 01:08:26,080
I did not ask her to fight.

1234
01:08:26,170 --> 01:08:27,130
She's doing it on her own.

1235
01:08:27,540 --> 01:08:28,540
It's all the same!

1236
01:08:28,630 --> 01:08:30,210
Usually, they bring along henchmen.

1237
01:08:30,380 --> 01:08:31,710
But you have your wife as your henchman.

1238
01:08:32,000 --> 01:08:33,000
Moron!

1239
01:08:52,210 --> 01:08:53,210
Oh, God!

1240
01:09:01,170 --> 01:09:03,750
-Let go!
-Does it hurt?

1241
01:09:39,290 --> 01:09:41,120
Hey, what are you waiting for?

1242
01:09:41,210 --> 01:09:42,250
Start the music!

1243
01:10:31,340 --> 01:10:32,970
Hey, what did you comment on that day?

1244
01:10:33,040 --> 01:10:34,460
I said you look voluptuous!

1245
01:10:36,920 --> 01:10:39,340
-How do you find my punch?
-It's hard-hitting!

1246
01:10:40,380 --> 01:10:41,460
Oh, God!

1247
01:10:44,880 --> 01:10:45,920
Hey, don't do it!

1248
01:10:47,090 --> 01:10:49,550
How many times did you watch Malena?

1249
01:10:49,630 --> 01:10:50,760
Five times!

1250
01:10:50,960 --> 01:10:54,090
One, two, three, four, five!

1251
01:10:57,290 --> 01:10:58,920
You managed to save your husband today.

1252
01:10:59,130 --> 01:11:02,170
But one day, we will kill him!

1253
01:11:04,130 --> 01:11:08,090
Hey, you have to deal with me first
to get to my husband.

1254
01:11:08,420 --> 01:11:09,500
I dare you!

1255
01:11:19,630 --> 01:11:20,960
She's valorous!

1256
01:11:24,380 --> 01:11:25,510
She's valorous!

1257
01:11:28,130 --> 01:11:29,170
Come on, let's go.

1258
01:11:39,420 --> 01:11:40,420
Hop on.

1259
01:11:53,250 --> 01:11:54,580
She's valorous!

1260
01:12:12,210 --> 01:12:13,710
Hey, change the channel.

1261
01:12:14,630 --> 01:12:15,630
HEADLINES

1262
01:12:15,750 --> 01:12:16,790
The weather today…

1263
01:12:16,960 --> 01:12:21,420
Son, you're married to a Wonder Woman!

1264
01:12:21,540 --> 01:12:24,790
Hereafter, no one would
dare mess with you.

1265
01:12:24,920 --> 01:12:25,960
Cheers!

1266
01:12:27,380 --> 01:12:28,300
Where are you leaving?

1267
01:12:29,210 --> 01:12:32,210
I desired to wed a girl
with the town's longest hair.

1268
01:12:32,340 --> 01:12:36,170
The bitter truth is
that my wife has the shortest hair.

1269
01:12:37,000 --> 01:12:38,420
She deceived me.

1270
01:12:38,960 --> 01:12:40,790
She humiliated me in front of the village.

1271
01:12:41,090 --> 01:12:43,630
-I ought to…
-Hold on! Sit down.

1272
01:12:44,590 --> 01:12:45,670
-Why?
-Sit. I'll explain.

1273
01:12:46,250 --> 01:12:48,130
You can go home after watching this.

1274
01:12:48,750 --> 01:12:49,880
For your safety.

1275
01:12:51,170 --> 01:12:52,050
Who is this boy?

1276
01:12:53,340 --> 01:12:54,920
I think you're too high.

1277
01:12:55,130 --> 01:12:56,630
Watch closely. That's your wife.

1278
01:12:58,340 --> 01:12:59,920
-Keerthi?
-Yes!

1279
01:13:00,460 --> 01:13:01,590
Your wife is a wrestler.

1280
01:13:02,290 --> 01:13:03,250
What is a wrestler?

1281
01:13:03,460 --> 01:13:04,840
She's a kusthi champion.

1282
01:13:05,380 --> 01:13:07,420
-Kusthi?
-Watch this video.

1283
01:13:10,380 --> 01:13:11,260
Hey, hey!

1284
01:13:11,380 --> 01:13:12,670
Not only that, 

1285
01:13:12,750 --> 01:13:15,080
your wife is a BSc graduate.

1286
01:13:17,460 --> 01:13:19,420
Does BSc mean she's more educated
than me?

1287
01:13:19,540 --> 01:13:20,580
A bit more educated than you.

1288
01:13:21,210 --> 01:13:23,000
I kept saying that I remembered

1289
01:13:23,090 --> 01:13:24,920
your wife from somewhere.

1290
01:13:25,040 --> 01:13:25,870
Yes!

1291
01:13:26,340 --> 01:13:27,630
I remember her from this video.

1292
01:13:27,960 --> 01:13:29,340
I even liked and commented on the video.

1293
01:13:29,880 --> 01:13:31,210
The guy who married her is doomed.

1294
01:13:31,920 --> 01:13:33,130
But never did I think

1295
01:13:33,210 --> 01:13:34,920
that you'll be her husband.

1296
01:13:35,380 --> 01:13:36,340
I'm very sorry!

1297
01:13:36,750 --> 01:13:40,420
The men your wife beat up
have been admitted to the hospital.

1298
01:13:40,840 --> 01:13:42,880
Doctors are stunned and mentioned

1299
01:13:43,000 --> 01:13:45,040
that only a person outraged and drenched

1300
01:13:45,170 --> 01:13:47,000
in violence can beat up like this.

1301
01:13:47,290 --> 01:13:49,460
Only four men can walk.

1302
01:13:50,090 --> 01:13:51,050
The ones you fought.

1303
01:13:52,090 --> 01:13:53,550
A brave woman who saved

1304
01:13:53,630 --> 01:13:55,340
her husband from the rowdies.

1305
01:13:55,460 --> 01:13:57,500
This exciting incident took place
in Pollachi.

1306
01:13:58,420 --> 01:14:01,880
During the temple carnival in Pollachi…

1307
01:14:02,290 --> 01:14:03,620
All they need is one piece of news.

1308
01:14:03,790 --> 01:14:04,790
They'll play it on a loop

1309
01:14:04,880 --> 01:14:05,960
to humiliate the person.

1310
01:14:06,340 --> 01:14:07,720
What are you doing over here?

1311
01:14:08,040 --> 01:14:09,290
Where else do you expect me to go?

1312
01:14:09,380 --> 01:14:10,340
When you get whacked!

1313
01:14:10,460 --> 01:14:11,380
I'll end up here.

1314
01:14:11,500 --> 01:14:12,540
Does your wife beat you?

1315
01:14:12,710 --> 01:14:14,290
All the wives tend to beat up
their husbands.

1316
01:14:14,460 --> 01:14:15,460
But that's domestic beating.

1317
01:14:15,750 --> 01:14:18,960
But his wife is dangerous!

1318
01:14:19,170 --> 01:14:23,210
Listen, they have started
the Husbands Protection Committee.

1319
01:14:23,500 --> 01:14:24,920
I have become a member.

1320
01:14:25,290 --> 01:14:27,870
If you join now
with the publicity you have attracted, 

1321
01:14:28,040 --> 01:14:29,960
they will make you
the ambassador of the committee.

1322
01:14:30,040 --> 01:14:32,040
-Our protection is important.
-Yes! Yes!

1323
01:14:32,130 --> 01:14:34,630
Hey, I'm not scared of my wife, 
unlike you.

1324
01:14:34,750 --> 01:14:36,040
Of course!

1325
01:14:36,210 --> 01:14:38,540
I'm pissed off.
It's better you go now.

1326
01:14:42,750 --> 01:14:44,080
Hey, hey, hey!

1327
01:14:44,540 --> 01:14:46,790
-My wife is calling!
-Answer the call.

1328
01:14:47,090 --> 01:14:48,720
-How do I speak?
-Like this!

1329
01:14:48,790 --> 01:14:50,080
-Bloody!
-Hello!

1330
01:14:50,170 --> 01:14:52,000
-Hello, 
-Where are you? Are you busy?

1331
01:14:52,250 --> 01:14:54,380
I'm not busy. I'm nearby.

1332
01:14:54,670 --> 01:14:56,130
I was speaking to my friends.

1333
01:14:56,250 --> 01:14:58,130
-When will you be home?
-I'll be there in ten minutes.

1334
01:14:58,210 --> 01:14:59,090
I'll hang up.

1335
01:14:59,170 --> 01:15:00,800
Bye. Bye!

1336
01:15:01,290 --> 01:15:02,420
Okay, dear.

1337
01:15:04,710 --> 01:15:07,000
First thing in the morning, 
join the committee.

1338
01:15:08,250 --> 01:15:09,380
Annoying man!

1339
01:15:10,130 --> 01:15:11,300
Hey, where's your bag?

1340
01:15:11,380 --> 01:15:12,300
Why do you need my bag?

1341
01:15:12,420 --> 01:15:14,170
-Give me your bag!
-What are you doing?

1342
01:15:14,630 --> 01:15:19,050
THE LAW WILL DO ITS DUTY

1343
01:15:19,130 --> 01:15:20,630
Hey, that's my toothbrush.

1344
01:15:21,090 --> 01:15:22,050
I don't mind!

1345
01:15:26,340 --> 01:15:28,130
-Okay, bye.
-Wait one minute.

1346
01:15:29,340 --> 01:15:30,420
Watch this before you leave.

1347
01:15:30,880 --> 01:15:32,760
Only then I'll be thrilled.

1348
01:15:34,210 --> 01:15:35,920
I'd remain the same
even after my marriage.

1349
01:15:53,540 --> 01:15:54,460
Keerthi, dear.

1350
01:15:56,960 --> 01:15:58,090
Keerthi, dear.

1351
01:16:02,710 --> 01:16:03,710
Come in.

1352
01:16:20,500 --> 01:16:22,830
My body is aching from the fight.

1353
01:16:23,540 --> 01:16:25,290
So, I could not cook today.

1354
01:16:25,840 --> 01:16:27,380
Please adjust tonight.

1355
01:16:27,500 --> 01:16:30,920
Come on. Even doctors recommend
leftover rice as the best body coolant.

1356
01:16:32,130 --> 01:16:33,760
I am okay with having this
for all my meals.

1357
01:16:34,880 --> 01:16:35,840
I…

1358
01:16:36,500 --> 01:16:37,960
I need to tell you one more thing.

1359
01:16:38,340 --> 01:16:39,220
Tell me!

1360
01:16:40,670 --> 01:16:41,920
I have short hair.

1361
01:16:42,000 --> 01:16:44,000
It's wrong of me to have hidden the truth.

1362
01:16:44,090 --> 01:16:45,260
-Do you know something?
-What?

1363
01:16:45,340 --> 01:16:47,470
Indira Gandhi had shorter hair.

1364
01:16:47,630 --> 01:16:49,090
Did she not become the Prime Minister?

1365
01:16:49,420 --> 01:16:51,630
Short hair looks good on you.

1366
01:16:55,710 --> 01:16:57,840
Also, I'm a BSc graduate.

1367
01:16:57,920 --> 01:16:58,880
That's great!

1368
01:16:59,000 --> 01:17:00,750
We don't have to put our kids
in coaching classes.

1369
01:17:00,880 --> 01:17:01,920
You can teach them.

1370
01:17:02,880 --> 01:17:05,130
Please pursue higher education.
I'll help you with it.

1371
01:17:05,210 --> 01:17:08,170
Because educating a girl
is educating a family.

1372
01:17:08,250 --> 01:17:10,960
-I also know…
-Wrestling, right?

1373
01:17:11,210 --> 01:17:12,420
The entire town saw your prowess!

1374
01:17:12,540 --> 01:17:13,580
You're great at it!

1375
01:17:13,670 --> 01:17:14,550
In these times, 

1376
01:17:14,630 --> 01:17:16,420
self-defense for women is vital.

1377
01:17:16,500 --> 01:17:17,540
Please pour some water.

1378
01:18:01,170 --> 01:18:03,130
Is she expecting me
to make the first move?

1379
01:18:03,540 --> 01:18:05,000
Would I get beaten if I made a move?

1380
01:18:05,540 --> 01:18:06,960
I'm confused!

1381
01:18:21,170 --> 01:18:22,090
What is it, uncle?

1382
01:18:22,290 --> 01:18:26,040
Son, this Puliyankolai council
is never-ending.

1383
01:18:26,340 --> 01:18:27,670
They have been dragging it out!

1384
01:18:28,420 --> 01:18:30,420
-Fine, I'll join you.
-Join us for what?

1385
01:18:30,790 --> 01:18:31,670
To the council.

1386
01:18:31,880 --> 01:18:33,010
You're well aware

1387
01:18:33,210 --> 01:18:35,210
that they're not afraid of anyone.

1388
01:18:35,380 --> 01:18:37,210
You tried many times to reason with them.

1389
01:18:37,290 --> 01:18:38,620
They don't seem to budge.

1390
01:18:38,710 --> 01:18:39,630
So?

1391
01:18:39,750 --> 01:18:42,880
So, we thought of taking your wife
along with us.

1392
01:18:43,380 --> 01:18:44,670
Also, we all believe

1393
01:18:44,750 --> 01:18:46,290
the verdict will be in our favor.

1394
01:18:46,420 --> 01:18:47,590
-My wife?
-Yes!

1395
01:18:49,840 --> 01:18:51,510
Sister, come on, let's go.

1396
01:18:51,960 --> 01:18:54,040
Oh, no! I'm not coming!

1397
01:18:54,170 --> 01:18:56,130
-Take him with you.
-You don't get it do you?

1398
01:18:56,250 --> 01:18:57,920
As it is, they never feared Veera.

1399
01:18:58,000 --> 01:18:59,250
Now, he's done for good!

1400
01:18:59,500 --> 01:19:00,670
Come on, dear, let's go!

1401
01:19:01,130 --> 01:19:03,550
Taking him along is the right thing to do.

1402
01:19:03,670 --> 01:19:05,210
I left the stove on. I have to cook.

1403
01:19:05,290 --> 01:19:07,290
Our partner Veera can beat up
the entire town.

1404
01:19:07,420 --> 01:19:09,460
Cooking food is child's play for him.

1405
01:19:10,380 --> 01:19:12,590
Partner, today you're the cook!

1406
01:19:12,670 --> 01:19:15,550
We'll get to taste your cooking
after the council meeting.

1407
01:19:16,460 --> 01:19:19,590
Listen, I put out clothes to wash.

1408
01:19:19,750 --> 01:19:21,960
-I need to wash them.
-Brother is good at wringing people.

1409
01:19:22,040 --> 01:19:23,250
Washing clothes is easy for him.

1410
01:19:23,340 --> 01:19:24,670
Brother, wash the clothes, 

1411
01:19:24,750 --> 01:19:26,170
put them to dry, and fold them.

1412
01:19:26,290 --> 01:19:27,370
It may rain today.

1413
01:19:30,040 --> 01:19:31,210
You see, I have to…

1414
01:19:37,290 --> 01:19:39,710
I was right.
To him, people are paramount.

1415
01:19:39,840 --> 01:19:41,010
He won't mind.

1416
01:19:41,090 --> 01:19:42,510
Come on! Please get inside the car.

1417
01:19:49,960 --> 01:19:51,960
Why are you carrying it?
Hold this for her.

1418
01:19:53,000 --> 01:19:54,130
Let's go. We're running late.

1419
01:19:55,960 --> 01:19:58,630
It is your wife's first time going to
the council meeting.

1420
01:19:58,750 --> 01:20:00,380
Why aren't you bidding her goodbye?

1421
01:20:01,460 --> 01:20:02,750
Come on, do it, son!

1422
01:20:03,130 --> 01:20:04,130
After all, it's just goodbye!

1423
01:20:23,790 --> 01:20:25,210
-Greetings, madam!
-Greetings, madam!

1424
01:20:28,130 --> 01:20:32,380
To bell the cat
She has come as a tiger

1425
01:20:32,750 --> 01:20:37,130
Like sugarcane to an elephant
One guy has gotten caught

1426
01:20:37,290 --> 01:20:39,670
If you enslave a girl
Not gonna happen

1427
01:20:39,840 --> 01:20:42,130
The boy shuddered
Enough!

1428
01:20:42,210 --> 01:20:44,500
The girl showed her strength
That's awesome!

1429
01:20:44,630 --> 01:20:46,880
The boy shivered

1430
01:20:47,340 --> 01:20:51,630
She is valorous
And can fight one-on-one

1431
01:20:52,090 --> 01:20:56,550
She took a wooden block
And swirled

1432
01:21:07,960 --> 01:21:08,960
She's valorous

1433
01:21:10,340 --> 01:21:11,260
She's valorous

1434
01:21:11,380 --> 01:21:13,550
Wearing gloves
Showing her arms' strength

1435
01:21:13,630 --> 01:21:16,010
She is going to win
You chauvinist cutie

1436
01:21:16,130 --> 01:21:18,800
Hit back the person
Who came to suppress you

1437
01:21:18,880 --> 01:21:21,170
Shave off his curled mustache

1438
01:21:24,250 --> 01:21:25,500
Please name my child.

1439
01:21:28,040 --> 01:21:29,670
-What are you doing?
-Naming your child.

1440
01:21:29,750 --> 01:21:32,960
You named my four other children.
And they're loitering hopeless!

1441
01:21:33,090 --> 01:21:34,420
You, please give the child
to your wife.

1442
01:21:34,710 --> 01:21:37,040
-They want you to name the child.
-Oh, is it?

1443
01:21:37,340 --> 01:21:38,470
GOVERNMENT SCHOOL

1444
01:21:44,960 --> 01:21:49,340
Who placed pride
Inside the dress of a woman?

1445
01:21:49,540 --> 01:21:54,420
Oh, does the culture get spoiled
If we cut our hair?

1446
01:21:57,210 --> 01:21:58,840
Get lost, you guys

1447
01:21:59,130 --> 01:22:03,880
They kept men in the front
And women at the back

1448
01:22:03,960 --> 01:22:06,340
They made the women
Who used to drive away tigers

1449
01:22:06,420 --> 01:22:08,670
Spin baskets
To keep the chicken safe

1450
01:22:08,750 --> 01:22:12,290
The people who try to enslave us
Should run away

1451
01:22:12,380 --> 01:22:13,510
Run, run, run, you guys

1452
01:22:13,630 --> 01:22:17,880
Are we here with you
To broom the floor?

1453
01:22:18,340 --> 01:22:23,090
After going around
He got caught by the right woman

1454
01:22:23,170 --> 01:22:27,630
Thinking he was hurting the ant
He hurt the lion's tooth

1455
01:22:27,880 --> 01:22:32,170
She is valorous
And can fight one-on-one

1456
01:22:32,460 --> 01:22:36,630
She took a wooden block
And swirled

1457
01:22:38,340 --> 01:22:41,090
Madam should come
and inaugurate our textile shop.

1458
01:22:44,710 --> 01:22:47,040
-Madam, are you planning to join politics?
-No!

1459
01:22:48,500 --> 01:22:50,750
Hey, who's that in the frame?
Get out of the frame.

1460
01:22:51,340 --> 01:22:52,630
Nonsense!
Go to your left!

1461
01:22:58,880 --> 01:23:01,380
We respectfully welcome

1462
01:23:01,540 --> 01:23:03,870
our mighty freedom fighter brother Ratnam!

1463
01:23:04,460 --> 01:23:07,250
Brother, now you're on the list
of freedom fighters.

1464
01:23:07,380 --> 01:23:08,260
Are you serious?

1465
01:23:08,380 --> 01:23:10,170
Everyone who serves a sentence
calls themselves one.

1466
01:23:10,250 --> 01:23:11,830
Why not you do the same?
It doesn't cost a dime.

1467
01:23:12,840 --> 01:23:14,340
Hey, where is my nephew?

1468
01:23:14,540 --> 01:23:15,670
Has he forgotten me after the marriage?

1469
01:23:15,750 --> 01:23:16,960
He didn't even come to receive me.

1470
01:23:17,090 --> 01:23:18,260
I'll explain everything later.

1471
01:23:20,920 --> 01:23:24,050
To sum up, Veera is roaming like a corpse.

1472
01:23:27,090 --> 01:23:28,760
It's he who is responsible for all of it.

1473
01:23:31,170 --> 01:23:32,050
Ratnam.

1474
01:23:32,290 --> 01:23:33,920
Ratnam, I heard you got out of prison.

1475
01:23:34,380 --> 01:23:35,960
I want to meet you right away.
Where are you?

1476
01:23:36,340 --> 01:23:38,550
I'm at Veera's house. Where are you?

1477
01:23:39,170 --> 01:23:41,000
Hey, go to Veera's house.

1478
01:23:43,420 --> 01:23:45,000
-Please eat.
-Fish curry, is it?

1479
01:23:45,250 --> 01:23:47,210
-Bring me fish fry.
-Sure, I'll get it.

1480
01:23:47,340 --> 01:23:48,510
Fry it well.

1481
01:23:50,590 --> 01:23:51,800
How do you sleep at night?

1482
01:23:51,920 --> 01:23:53,500
I trusted you and got my nephew married.

1483
01:23:53,840 --> 01:23:54,920
How could you betray me?

1484
01:23:57,420 --> 01:23:58,500
You seem very angry.

1485
01:23:58,590 --> 01:24:00,470
We should not discuss family matters
when we're angry.

1486
01:24:00,590 --> 01:24:01,670
Please sit down and have food.

1487
01:24:01,750 --> 01:24:03,670
-Keerthi made a mean fish curry--
-Hey!

1488
01:24:03,750 --> 01:24:05,210
Do you think I'm here to attend a feast?

1489
01:24:08,420 --> 01:24:09,920
Your folks did not have any sense.

1490
01:24:10,090 --> 01:24:12,130
And lied to get you married.

1491
01:24:12,250 --> 01:24:13,250
Don't you have any sense?

1492
01:24:13,340 --> 01:24:15,380
Ratnam, I'm the one to blame here.

1493
01:24:15,500 --> 01:24:16,420
Yell at me all you want.

1494
01:24:16,500 --> 01:24:17,500
Not her. She's a poor thing.

1495
01:24:17,670 --> 01:24:20,550
Hey, she's fighting like a rogue
on the streets.

1496
01:24:20,710 --> 01:24:23,130
-She's not a poor thing.
-Don't talk like a fool.

1497
01:24:23,420 --> 01:24:25,800
Had she not made it on time that day, 

1498
01:24:26,000 --> 01:24:27,130
they would've killed Veera.

1499
01:24:27,380 --> 01:24:29,380
It would've been better if he got killed.

1500
01:24:29,670 --> 01:24:34,630
It's better to get killed by an enemy
than saved by a woman.

1501
01:24:35,290 --> 01:24:37,830
My husband's life is more important
than your family's pride.

1502
01:24:37,960 --> 01:24:40,920
No woman would stay silent
when her husband is about to get killed.

1503
01:24:41,130 --> 01:24:42,210
Moreover, I'm a wrestler.

1504
01:24:42,380 --> 01:24:43,340
I will fight!

1505
01:24:43,460 --> 01:24:45,920
You should have raised her like a woman.

1506
01:24:46,000 --> 01:24:48,000
If you raise her like a man, she'll fight.

1507
01:24:48,210 --> 01:24:49,420
Uncle, ask him to leave.

1508
01:24:49,500 --> 01:24:51,380
Hey, you don't have the right
to send me out.

1509
01:24:51,460 --> 01:24:52,420
Speak with respect.

1510
01:24:52,500 --> 01:24:54,790
Hey, this is how I speak to women.

1511
01:24:54,880 --> 01:24:56,010
You're not special!

1512
01:24:57,000 --> 01:25:00,130
It would be best if you raised a girl
to be modest and obedient.

1513
01:25:00,250 --> 01:25:02,210
If not, they'll talk back like a rogue!

1514
01:25:02,840 --> 01:25:05,170
Hey, Keerthi, what have you done?

1515
01:25:08,090 --> 01:25:11,470
How long will you keep up
the charade of moral policing women?

1516
01:25:11,750 --> 01:25:13,210
Don't we know how to lead our life?

1517
01:25:13,340 --> 01:25:14,590
Would you keep lecturing for life?

1518
01:25:14,710 --> 01:25:16,500
Hey, why did you slap him?

1519
01:25:17,290 --> 01:25:20,120
Male chauvinists like him
should be taught a lesson.

1520
01:25:20,340 --> 01:25:21,260
Ratnam!

1521
01:25:21,380 --> 01:25:22,590
Hey, Ratnam, please stop.

1522
01:25:22,750 --> 01:25:23,920
I said, stop!

1523
01:25:24,250 --> 01:25:26,580
She's innocent. It was a mistake.

1524
01:25:32,960 --> 01:25:34,670
-Hey, where is she?
-What happened?

1525
01:25:34,790 --> 01:25:36,540
She's inside. Hey!

1526
01:25:37,170 --> 01:25:39,130
Just because you're strong, 
you will beat anyone as you please?

1527
01:25:40,460 --> 01:25:42,290
Do you know your uncle disrespected me?

1528
01:25:42,380 --> 01:25:44,210
That doesn't give you the right
to slap him.

1529
01:25:44,340 --> 01:25:45,420
-Hear me out--
-Keerthi!

1530
01:25:45,960 --> 01:25:47,250
He is right.

1531
01:25:47,670 --> 01:25:49,420
No matter what, 
you should not have slapped him.

1532
01:25:49,540 --> 01:25:51,080
Come on, let's go and apologize to Ratnam.

1533
01:25:51,290 --> 01:25:52,420
She will apologize to him.

1534
01:25:52,500 --> 01:25:54,420
An apology won't make things right.

1535
01:25:54,790 --> 01:25:56,250
I never said I'm going to apologize.

1536
01:25:56,380 --> 01:25:58,420
Please don't add fuel to the problem.

1537
01:25:58,630 --> 01:26:01,460
Apologizing once won't make us any lesser.
Let's go!

1538
01:26:01,540 --> 01:26:04,290
First, ask his uncle to apologize
for demeaning women.

1539
01:26:04,590 --> 01:26:06,420
After that, 
I'll apologize for slapping him.

1540
01:26:06,590 --> 01:26:07,470
What did you say?

1541
01:26:07,710 --> 01:26:10,130
You expect my uncle to apologize to you?

1542
01:26:10,340 --> 01:26:11,630
Such arrogance?

1543
01:26:12,170 --> 01:26:15,460
-This is not going to work.
-Veera… Listen…

1544
01:26:15,540 --> 01:26:18,620
Why are you being short with your in-laws?

1545
01:26:19,000 --> 01:26:20,960
I never said anything wrong.
You know me well.

1546
01:26:21,090 --> 01:26:23,220
A girl should never be short
with her in-laws.

1547
01:26:23,340 --> 01:26:25,090
Uncle, you do know how he spoke to me.

1548
01:26:25,540 --> 01:26:27,920
Hey, you don't belong
in this house anymore. Get out!

1549
01:26:28,090 --> 01:26:29,880
-Son, it was a mistake.
-Hey, get lost!

1550
01:26:30,000 --> 01:26:32,080
-It's all because of you.
-I agree it's me!

1551
01:26:32,170 --> 01:26:34,210
I beg of you not to do this.

1552
01:26:34,290 --> 01:26:36,420
-Let go!
-Don't throw her out of the house.

1553
01:26:36,540 --> 01:26:38,790
Uncle, you don't have to beg him.

1554
01:26:39,500 --> 01:26:41,830
He's not even ready
